# Stable spec ID: difford-sazerac. Source checked 2026-10-12. Machine generated; not human reviewed.

::ingredients
(rye whiskey; straight, 100 proof / 50% alc./vol.) 45 ml
(simple syrup, rich, 2 sugar to 1 water, 65.0°Brix) 7.5 ml
(bitters choice) = (bitters @ Peychaud's) 3 dashes -OR- (bitters; Creole-style) 3 dashes
(rinse spirit) = (absinthe @ La Fée Parisienne) 4 dashes -OR- (anise spirit @ Herbsaint)

::equipment
(rocks glass)
(mixing glass)

::instructions
(rocks glass) <fill, with ice> <set aside>
{drink} = (rye whiskey, straight, 100 proof / 50% alc./vol.) + (simple syrup, rich, 2 sugar to 1 water, 65.0°Brix) + (bitters choice)
{drink} <stir, with ice in (mixing glass)>
(rocks glass) <empty, discarding ice> <rinse, with the chosen (rinse spirit)>
{drink} <strain, into the prepared glass>
<express citrus oil, from lemon zest twist over the drink>
<garnish, with the same twist>

::notes
Strength of absinthe is not automatically strength of the rinse choice. The editorial method expressly permits Herbsaint.
Named products use bare @ unless a stronger intent is explicitly authored. No automatic substitution is implied.

